course: dictionary
lesson: 10222
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it. «But real toads walk slowly to their ponds instead of driving cars into them.» Toads walk and have ponds, so here toad is an animal.
explain: Toad has a second meaning too: an old insult for a nasty person. Look at the clues in «Toad thinks a long time and then says sadly...». Toad has a capital letter and does things a person does, so it is the name of a character, not an animal.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «a nasty person walks slowly to their ponds» make sense? No. So the animal meaning is the right one.
fact: A toad is a small animal like a frog, and it is an amphibian.
fact: Toads have dry, bumpy skin and short legs, so they walk or hop rather than leap.
fact: Toads lay their eggs in water as spawn, in strings. The eggs hatch into tadpoles, which grow legs and become toads.
fact: Many toads have poison glands, so never lick or eat one, and wash your hands after touching one.
fact: «Toad» can also be an old insult meaning a nasty person, and «Toad» is the name of a famous character in «The Wind in the Willows».
exercise: «Real toads walk slowly to their ponds.» In this sentence, what is a toad? | A kind of pond weed | A nasty person | *A small animal like a frog | A type of bird
exercise: Someone shouts, «You toad, you took my turn!» What does toad mean here? | A frog prince from a story | A small animal with dry, bumpy skin | A tadpole | *A nasty person
exercise: Toads start life as eggs in water. What do the eggs hatch into? | Frogs with wings | Birds | Fish | *Tadpoles
test: Why should you never lick or eat a toad? | Toads are always too big to lick | *Many toads have poison glands | Toads only like sweet food | Toads bite everyone who touches them
test: What tells you that «Toad» in «Toad thinks a long time» is a character name? | The word sadly at the end | The full stop at the end | *The capital letter T, and he does things a person does | The word long
exam: What is the best way to check which meaning of toad fits a sentence? | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense | Pick the first meaning you think of | Ignore the sentence and guess | Look only at the title
